  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When converting my avatar to the beta, it took roughly 25 minutes to finish calculating all of the animation paths, but most things seem to have worked correctly. However, I did have one auto conversion that resulted in a \"Missing Path\" in the animation.\n\nThe constraint in question is a parent constraint on my right eye with the position locks disabled (so it's basically just a rotation constraint). The same object also has a Position Constraint. There are 3 related animations where I am setting the Source Weights of the 2 sources.\n\nFor some reason, all connections to Element 0 are considered \"Missing\" and do not animate properly in any of the related animations. It is labeled as \"R_eye---HOLDER--- : managedReferences[3845849039442804740].Weight\" in the animation path.\n\nHowever, Element 1 is working as expected!\n\nAlso, my left eye has an identical setup, but everything converted correctly!\n\nAdmittedly this is pretty easy to fix, but it's difficult to track these down.\n\nIf I can provide any additional information, please let me know.",
